  "portal_description": "The MultiCloud Object Gateway provides a lightweight object store service, based on the NooBaa project. It connects to backing storage automatically and can easily scale on-premise, create hybrid cloud and multicloud storage, based on native cloud storage.\n\nThis enhancement update adds the Multicloud Object Gateway command-line interface, a tool that helps administrators to manage the deployment and second-day operations for the object service, such as adding backing stores, managing bucket claims, and setting mirroring and multicloud policies via bucket classes. It provides a friendly interface and produces YAML files for the operator in the background.",
  "lastModifiedDate": "2020-01-14T04:09:43Z",
  "resource_uri": "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHBA-2020:0098",
  "portal_publication_date": "2020-01-14T04:09:43Z",
  "portal_product_names": ["Red Hat OpenShift Data Foundation"],
  "abstract": "The MultiCloud Object Gateway provides a lightweight object store service, based on the NooBaa project. It connects to backing storage automatically and can easily scale on-premise, create hybrid cloud and multicloud storage, based on native cloud storage.\n\nThis enhancement update adds the Multicloud Object Gateway command-line interface, a tool that helps administrators to manage the deployment and second-day operations for the object service, such as adding backing stores, managing bucket claims, and setting mirroring and multicloud policies via bucket classes. It provides a friendly interface and produces YAML files for the operator in the background.",
